  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$",
  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{\u2032} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{\u2032} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)",
